YAAP - Nyet-Val-Dwa-Fem-Law : wishless genoless polyselfless polypileless
near-petless (angel on Astral, ignored) survivor

This was my first successful combat-wombat character (already ascended 2
W's and an M, and my P is going extinctionist.)  I had just played a
knight who died to Ixoth on the quest, having never found a bag of any
sort, or an altar outside Minetown.  I started this character intending to
ascend, but not thinking much about conducts.  Most of them I decided
mid-game.  She was also my first successful character to use the note
sheets at http://home.comcast.net/~tomandcatherine/ -- they turned out to
be VERY useful.

Nyet did not like pets, and in fact did not start with one.  She started
out by heading straight toward Sokoban, which was on DLVL 7.  About 5000
turns into the game she had a BoH, and also got poison resistance from a
guardian naga hatchling at the start of that level.  She dipped for
Excalibur, and then headed for the mines to price and BUC ID stuff.  Found
a magic marker in one of the shops, but the altar was crossaligned so no
saccing yet.  Avoided the levels below minetown for a bit, as she had no
source of MR and didn't want to step on any polytraps.  Got fire
resistance from a fire ant about this time, so was doing fairly well for
intrinsics.

She headed down the main dungeon, always on the edge of burdened, making
stashes along the way.  This was until she realized she had a !oHW from
the very early game... did I mention she wasn't too bright?  Int 8 at the
start, no wonder she didn't think to bless the bag ;)  She was also very
ugly -- sat on a throne and lost some charisma.  Got the message "you feel
very repulsive" as her cha dropped to 5!  But hey, she *was* strong, and
wielding Excalibur made her a force to be reckoned with.  So who cares how
ugly she was?

A rothe brought her a magic lamp, which she ID'd as uncursed and hung on
to as a light source.  A bones file on DLVL 9 yielded up another magic
marker and a cloak of MR (hooray for wizards!) so she headed toward mines
end.  AC-5 or so with all the dwarvish armor (mithril, boots, helm) plus
the starting shield and the CoMR.  Nothing very interesting happened until
DL20, where she found her very first useable altar, and got Mojo on the
first sac.  She kept using excalibur, though, for the most part (since it
was already +5.)

Crowning came fairly soon, but then she had to run away from the altar
when her wand of create sacrifice created about a dozen, including 4
soldiers and a couple trolls.  She headed upstairs badly in need of
reflection, and killed a peaceful aleax for his shield.  Messed around for
about 20,000 turns trying to get stronger and looking for more equipment
(finished the quest fairly easily in this time) but couldn't find an easy
way to cross medusa.  Eventually discovered a =oTC and started eating tins
of leprechaun, and then did the black pudding thing waiting for more rings
to show up.  30 AC later, she had an amulet of magical breathing and a
couple wands of cold, so headed for medusa.  The first (and only) hostile
tengu of the game showed up, and she finally felt in control, so her rings
now became slow digestion and +3 increase damage.

The castle went down fairly quickly to a rubber chicken (lich summoned it
and quickly regretted doing so) but she still couldn't levitate to get to
the dragons in the back of the castle, and wasn't particularly interested
in their scales anyway (2 orange, a blue, and a white IIRC.)  So she went
looking around everywhere, including on the quest, and ended up in the
lava due to the buggy travel command (and also discovered another bug
after freezing the floor and surrounding area -- zapped a /oDig down, and
was still stuck in the floor.  Took a couple more zaps to finally fall
through.)  Curse geno'd silver dragons for some scales, dropped the shield
of reflection, and started #twoweaponing Excalibur and a +3 longsword from
the aforementioned friendly Aleax whose shield had been so helpful.

Within 2000 turns, 2 more silver dragons (randomly generated) dropped
scales.  And my wife's atheist wizards keep getting 4 altars before level
10.  I should start declaring "wishless" so the RNG will give me 8
/oWishing early game, and then I'll break the conduct ;)  A prayer at the
altar yielded a spellbook of identify, which came in handy for the rest of
the game (though she had to take off her GoP to cast it.)  She ID'd a ring
of levitation, and headed down to Gehennom fairly well equipped (AC -50,
SDSM, CoMR, GoP, elven helm, T-shirt).  She decided to try for wishless
and genoless at this point, opting to leave the 0:2 wand of wishing alone
and hang on to the magic lamp.  Juiblex showed up in the valley of the
dead, where he joined the dead at the hands of the +6 excalibur and +5
longsword.  Asmodeus (level 36) summoned all 3 Erinys over the course of 2
turns, and then Baalzebub, Dispater, and Geryon.  They all died fairly
quickly.

Orcustown (39) wasn't terribly interesting.  Shades went down quickly to
Excalibur and a longsword due to the +3 ring and +6 strength bonus.  Nyet
built a boulder fort around the stairs and then woke up Orcus, who
summoned Yeenoghu.  Only one major demon left... and the big D showed up
about 5 turns later.  AC -50 is where Demogorgon starts to miss, so he
went down fairly quickly and only made her sick 2-3 times.

Vlad's tower was on level 42, and had the first AoLS all game.  She never
put it on, opting to stick with the ESP she'd found early game.  Took
dagger to expert (should've done this a long time ago) to go with expert
longsword and skilled twoweaponing.  Mojo and the daggers became her
anti-mindflayer / anti-eel attack.  She also named a ring "#9" about this
time.

Wasted a bunch more turns looking for an oilskin sack and a ring of free
action and an interesting helmet, but with no luck.  Considered breaking
wishless but decided against it.  So she marked the vibrating square (
http://home.comcast.net/~tomandcatherine/vsquare.gif ) and dropped the
Candelabrum and Bell there, and then woke up Rodney.  He didn't last too
long against the +7 Excalibur, +7 longsword, +3 ring of increase damage,
and +6 from the GoP.  Averaged over 50 damage per shot.  The high priest
went down to a /oDeath, and the amulet was named and ID'd appropriately.

The end game was fairly uninteresting.  The mysterious force didn't hit at
all from the sanctum (50) up to level 43, when my wife commented on it.
The next 3 staircases went 43->46->46->48.  Also 45->45, 44->44,
43->45->45, 39->40->42, 34->34->37, 32->32->33, and finally got back to
the castle.

Earth was simple -- a scroll of gold detection revealed the portal, and
about 5 digging charges was all it took.  On air, Nyet wanted to wear her
ring of levitation -- but her gloves were cursed.  A prayer resulted in
Tyr being "well pleased", so she had to get out some holy water.  (She
carried her BoH inside another sack, both greased, and had a third sack
further inside which was also greased.  Each layer had some holy water, so
that a water accident wouldn't take it *all* out.)  Being lawful, the
archon on air wasn't any trouble -- he just stood there and smiled ;)  Air
elementals weren't so dangerous with the orb of fate and 800-ish hitpoints
(a bit of alchemy, and then just drank every potion anything dropped.)
Fire was easy after a couple zaps of cold made bridges, and she put on an
amulet of magical breathing for water, but never needed it.  The orb of
fate detected the portals on air, fire, and water (and a wand of secret
door detection did some supplemental re-detects on water.)

On astral, she got a pet angel (but never used him -- just walked away and
left him behind.)  Famine was in the middle, and probably the least
dangerous since she had 9 blessed lumps of royal jelly left over (giants
had put her strength where she wanted it.)  Famine died in 2 hits, and
never landed one of his own.  Then she pushed through the crowd and
discovered the lawful altar of Tyr... she's the h standing on the altar
(dropped into text mode to get an end-game capture.  Normally play
tiles...)


